{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFTWS85QxBYBcUFPAGpn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I merged the day 21 metadata and warmups codecs and one web fact into lib/, and rejected one proposal. The ratchet gate (`ratchet-gate day21`) is green. It failed once first because my new test expected the wrong decoded text for a sample (`nice w` instead of `nyx-56`); I fixed the test, not lib, and nothing was committed.\n\n1. **Metadata:** new module `lib/meta/apk.py`, registered as verified for day 21 under `(\"apk\", \"package_name\")`. It reads the `package` attribute from the APK's binary AndroidManifest.xml using only the standard library, and falls back to androguard if that fails. It gives `com.huntress.arena.p08281778` on the single, the time trial and all 5 Mastery sets, and matches androguard on 60 APKs in the repo.\n2. **Warmups:** added day 21 `b64-gzip` to `lib/warmups_codecs.py` `DAYS`. It's standard base64 of gzip at level 9 with the `Z_FILTERED` strategy, which reproduces the single, time trial and 103/103 Mastery line-21 blobs byte for byte (Python's default gzip settings don't match on the full sentence). `lib.decode.decode_chunk` gained a matching branch for base64 of gzip, zlib, bz2 or xz, only active from day 21. It isn't a free-text codec, so `FREE_CODECS` is unchanged.\n3. **Web (merged):** the reflect-upon-this rule went into `lib/knowledge.py` as `WEB_XSS_CLUE_ROUTE_KEYS`: pick the XSS callback route by its `/api/clues` key (`secondary_route`), not by the word in its path. The GM accepted it on both the single (`/callback-77e6ec`) and the time trial (`/internal-8c5b43`). `lib/playbook.py` is unchanged because it only holds answer-label spelling rules, and this isn't one.\n4. **Web (rejected):** `lib.web.compound_probe` from stored-for-later. It's a chain of exploit probes, i.e. solver code, and lib/ only takes facts, codecs and helper branches, so the import cycle between the web day solvers stays theirs to fix. The binary, script and mobile days needed nothing new: the GitHub Actions host was already handled by `lib/codec.py`, and binary's day 21 member choice lives in its own solver.\n5. **Tests:** three new checks at the end of `tests/test_day7_fixes.py` (the D21 codec and its decode branch, apk `package_name`, the web route key). No existing assertion was changed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":400,"cache_read_input_tokens":110065,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":400},"output_tokens":798,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cd6e6acb-75d1-49cf-8da4-c3379eb4e6e0","uuid":"dc5c3489-8e19-4f29-93b3-62686129f172","timestamp":"2026-10-21T13:25:59.021Z","request_id":"req_011CgFTWRpUS2nmfUVnQMEYa"}
